"></path></svg></div><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">RS=
S ensures the NIC hardware itself places packets from the same 5-tuple flow=
 into a specific RX queue. This queue maps to a specific CPU core via MSI-X=
 interrupts. Our software will bind one thread per RSS queue.</span></p></l=
i><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Disable P=
rotocol Offloads:</span></strong><span class=3D""></span><br><span class=3D=
"">TCP/UDP Checksum Offloading and Large Send Offload (LSO) must be disable=
d. They modify the packet in hardware, so the captured data would not be th=
e wire-format bytes. Our behavioral system needs raw IP/TCP headers exactly=
 as sent.</span></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=
=3D"">In the same NIC Advanced Tab: Disable all </span><code>Offload</code>=
<span class=3D""> settings (TCP Checksum Offload IPv4/IPv6, UDP Checksum Of=
fload, Large Send Offload).</span></p></li></ul></li></ol><hr><h2><span cla=
ss=3D"">3. Software Architecture &amp; Thread Model</span></h2><p class=3D"=
ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">The acquisition process runs as a <=
/span><strong><span class=3D"">Windows Service</span></strong><span class=
=3D""> (</span><code>CaptureSvc.exe</code><span class=3D"">) to survive use=
r logoffs and run under a dedicated high-priority account (e.g., </span><co=
de>NT SERVICE\NetworkCapture</code><span class=3D"">).</span></p><p class=
=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">The internal workflow is a </sp=
an><strong><span class=3D"">producer-consumer pipeline with lock-free queue=
s</span></strong><span class=3D"">.</span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-parag=
raph"><strong><span class=3D"">Thread Layout:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p=
 class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Main Control Thre=
ad:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Initializes Npcap, opens the adapter, =
sets up ring buffers, spawns capture threads, and handles shutdown signals.=
</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=
=3D"">Capture Threads (N =3D Number of RSS Queues):</span></strong><span cl=
ass=3D""> Each thread is affinitized to a specific CPU core. It runs a tigh=
t loop calling </span><code>pcap_dispatch()</code><span class=3D""> or the =
zero-copy </span><code>pcap_next_ex()</code><span class=3D""> on its dedica=
ted packet buffer. This thread does </span><em><span class=3D"">no processi=
ng</span></em><span class=3D"">, only timestamp annotation and enqueue.</sp=
an></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D""=
>Dispatch Thread:</span></strong><span class=3D""> A dedicated writer threa=
d that drains the packet ring buffer and writes batched blocks to shared me=
mory (the IPC mechanism to Layer 2). It runs on a separate core to avoid ca=
che line bouncing with capture threads.</span></p></li></ul><hr><h2><span c=
lass=3D"">4. Detailed Runtime Workflow</span></h2><h3><span class=3D"">Phas=
e A: Initialization Sequence</span></h3><ol start=3D"1"><li><p class=3D"ds-=
markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Start Service Control Dispatch=
er:</span></strong><span class=3D""> The SCM starts </span><code>CaptureSvc=
.exe</code><span class=3D"">. </span><code>main()</code><span class=3D""> c=
alls </span><code>StartServiceCtrlDispatcher()</code><span class=3D"">.</sp=
an></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D""=
>Set Privileges:</span></strong><span class=3D""> The service thread calls =
</span><code>AdjustTokenPrivileges</code><span class=3D""> to acquire </spa=
n><code>SeLoadDriverPrivilege</code><span class=3D""> (needed by Npcap=E2=
=80=99s LWF driver communication) and </span><code>SeLockMemoryPrivilege</c=
ode><span class=3D""> (for locking the page-aligned ring buffer memory, pre=
venting it from being paged to disk).</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-mar=
kdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Find Adapter:</span></strong><spa=
n class=3D""> </span><code>pcap_findalldevs()</code><span class=3D""> is ca=
lled. The result list is filtered to find the specific adapter by its perma=
nent GUID (hardcoded in the service config), ignoring the loopback and MS T=
unnel adapters.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><stro=
ng><span class=3D"">Create Ring Buffer (Shared Memory):</span></strong></p>=
<ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">The service cre=
ates a named </span><strong><span class=3D"">memory-mapped file</span></str=
ong><span class=3D""> object: </span><code>Local\CognitiveFW_CaptureBuffer<=
/code><span class=3D"">.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragra=
ph"><span class=3D"">Size is fixed (e.g., 1 GB), a power of 2 for efficient=
 index masking.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span=
 class=3D"">The layout is a contiguous block holding an array of packet des=
criptor structs followed by raw packet data.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D=
"ds-markdown-paragraph"><code>VirtualAlloc</code><span class=3D""> with </s=
pan><code>MEM_LARGE_PAGES</code><span class=3D""> is attempted to use 2MB p=
ages for better TLB efficiency. Falls back to standard 4KB pages if not con=
figured in Group Policy.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdo=
wn-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Prepare Synchronization Primitives:<=
/span></strong></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=
=3D"">Two named semaphores: </span><code>Local\CognitiveFW_PacketReady_Sem<=
/code><span class=3D""> (Producer, initially 0) and </span><code>Local\Cogn=
itiveFW_FreeSlots_Sem</code><span class=3D""> (Consumer, initially </span><=
code>buffer_size</code><span class=3D"">).</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"d=
s-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">A control event: </span><code>Local\=
CognitiveFW_Shutdown_Event</code><span class=3D""> (Manual-reset).</span></=
p></li></ul></li></ol><h3><span class=3D"">Phase B: Per-Capture-Thread Star=
t</span></h3><ol start=3D"1"><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong=
><span class=3D"">Spawn Thread:</span></strong><span class=3D""> For each R=
SS queue index </span><code>i</code><span class=3D""> (0 to 3), the main th=
read spawns a capture thread, passing </span><code>i</code><span class=3D""=
> as a parameter.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><st=
rong><span class=3D"">Set Affinity Mask:</span></strong><span class=3D""> T=
he capture thread calls </span><code>SetThreadAffinityMask</code><span clas=
s=3D""> to bind itself to CPU core </span><code>i + BaseProcessorNumber</co=
de><span class=3D"">. It also sets its priority to </span><code>THREAD_PRIO=
RITY_TIME_CRITICAL</code><span class=3D""> (15).</span></p></li><li><p clas=
s=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Open Independent pcap =
Handle:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Each thread opens a </span><strong=
><span class=3D"">separate</span></strong><span class=3D""> </span><code>pc=
ap_t</code><span class=3D""> handle on the </span><em><span class=3D"">same=
 adapter</span></em><span class=3D"">, but configured to receive only from =
RSS queue </span><code>i</code><span class=3D""> via a specific Npcap API c=
all (</span><code>pcap_set_rfmon</code><span class=3D""> or a vendor extens=
ion to set the queue). </span><em><span class=3D"">Note: This capability is=
 available in Npcap's premium OEM edition; the free version uses a single h=
andle and software dispatch. The OEM workflow is described here for archite=
ctural fidelity.</span></em></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"=
><strong><span class=3D"">Set Timestamp Mode:</span></strong><span class=3D=
""> </span><code>pcap_set_tstamp_precision(handle, PCAP_TSTAMP_PRECISION_NA=
NO)</code><span class=3D""> is called. This forces Npcap to use the NIC=E2=
=80=99s hardware timestamping (if available) or the QueryPerformanceCounter=
 (QPC)-based software timestamp with hardware-synchronized accuracy.</span>=
</p></li></ol><h3><span class=3D"">Phase C: Steady-State Capture Loop (The =
Core)</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">This i=
s a continuous, unbounded loop on each capture thread.</span></p><div class=
