Extractor (The CNN Bridge)</span></strong><span class=3D""> on Windows 10.<=
/span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">This layer is=
 the critical transformation point where </span><strong><span class=3D"">ra=
w network metadata becomes a mathematical object a CNN can understand</span=
></strong><span class=3D"">. Its output is not a classification, but a stan=
dardized tensor ready for inference.</span></p><hr><h2><span class=3D"">1. =
Core Concept &amp; Mathematical Foundation</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-markdo=
wn-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Before tools, understand the transformation:=
</span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">A flow's pac=
ket sequence is a 1D time series with multiple channels: </span><code>[time=
stamp, direction, length, flags, TTL]</code><span class=3D"">. A CNN expect=
s a fixed-size 2D image-like structure: </span><code>Height =C3=97 Width =
=C3=97 Channels</code><span class=3D"">.</span></p><p class=3D"ds-markdown-=
paragraph"><span class=3D"">The fundamental job of Layer 3 is a </span><str=
ong><span class=3D"">lossy, structured projection</span></strong><span clas=
s=3D""> from variable-length time series =E2=86=92 fixed-size multi-channel=
 matrix. This is not simple resizing; it is statistical aggregation within =
grid cells that preserves behavioral patterns.</span></p><p class=3D"ds-mar=
kdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Why this works for security:</spa=
n></strong></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">=
A C2 beacon shows as vertical stripes in the time axis (periodic bursts).</=
span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">DNS t=
unneling shows as high-entropy horizontal bands in the packet size channel.=
</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Por=
t scanning shows as a sparse, wide-directional pattern.</span></p></li><li>=
<p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">These are visually dist=
inct "textures" that CNN convolutional filters detect.</span></p></li></ul>=
<hr><h2><span class=3D"">2. Tools, Frameworks &amp; Dependencies</span></h2=
