g></div><h3><span class=3D"">Step 4: Model File Deployment</span></h3><p cl=
ass=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">The </span><code>.pt</code><=
span class=3D""> or </span><code>.trt</code><span class=3D""> file, along w=
ith a </span><code>model_manifest.json</code><span class=3D""> (version, ch=
ecksum, input shape, normalization parameters), is placed in </span><code>C=
:\ProgramData\CognitiveFW\models\</code><span class=3D"">. The service load=
s the latest version on startup.</span></p><hr><h2><span class=3D"">5. Thre=
ad Architecture</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=
=3D"">Layer 4 runs as </span><code>InferenceEngineSvc.exe</code><span class=
=3D""> with a </span><strong><span class=3D"">pipeline parallelism</span></=
strong><span class=3D""> design.</span></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-=
paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Batch Collector Thread (1x):</span></st=
rong><span class=3D""> Reads individual tensors from Layer 3's shared memor=
y. Accumulates them into a </span><strong><span class=3D"">dynamic batch</s=
pan></strong><span class=3D"">. Does not perform inference.</span></p></li>=
<li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">GPU Inferen=
ce Thread (1x):</span></strong><span class=3D""> The only thread that calls=
 LibTorch. Waits for a batch to be ready or a timeout. Executes forward pas=
s on GPU. Distributes individual results back.</span></p></li><li><p class=
=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">XAI Post-Processor Thre=
ad (1x, Conditional):</span></strong><span class=3D""> Only spawned if Grad=
-CAM is enabled. Computes heatmaps for a sampled subset of flows flagged as=
 malicious (not all, due to computational cost).</span></p></li><li><p clas=
s=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Verdict Dispatcher Thr=
ead (1x):</span></strong><span class=3D""> Takes completed </span><code>Inf=
erenceResult</code><span class=3D""> structs, serializes them via protobuf,=
 writes to output shared memory (</span><code>Local\CognitiveFW_VerdictExpo=
rt</code><span class=3D"">), signals Layer 5.</span></p></li></ul><p class=
=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Why only one GPU thread=
?</span></strong><span class=3D""></span><br><span class=3D"">GPU inference=
 is massively parallel within a batch. Multiple threads competing for the G=
PU would cause context switching overhead on the CUDA streams. A single thr=
ead submitting well-formed batches saturates the GPU efficiently. For multi=
-GPU systems, one thread per GPU is used.</span></p><hr><h2><span class=3D"=
">6. Detailed Runtime Workflow</span></h2><h3><span class=3D"">Phase A: Ini=
tialization</span></h3><ol start=3D"1"><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragrap=
h"><strong><span class=3D"">GPU Selection &amp; Warmup:</span></strong></p>=
<ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">LibTorch select=
s the GPU with the most free memory via </span><code>torch::cuda::is_availa=
ble()</code><span class=3D""> and explicit device index.</span></p></li><li=
><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Load the TorchScript m=
odel: </span><code>torch::jit::load("cognitive_fw_cnn.pt")</code><span clas=
s=3D"">.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span class=
=3D"">Move model to GPU: </span><code>model-&gt;to(torch::kCUDA)</code><spa=
n class=3D"">.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><stron=
g><span class=3D"">Warmup Pass:</span></strong><span class=3D""> Run 10 inf=
erences on random </span><code>[4, 32, 32]</code><span class=3D""> tensors.=
 This triggers CUDA kernel compilation, cuDNN convolution algorithm selecti=
on (autotuning), and GPU memory allocation. Without warmup, the first real =
inference would take 100-500ms instead of 1-3ms.</span></p></li></ul></li><=
li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Attach Input=
 Shared Memory:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragrap=
h"><span class=3D"">Opens </span><code>Local\CognitiveFW_TensorExport</code=
><span class=3D""> (from Layer 3).</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdo=
wn-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Maps the protobuf schema.</span></p></li></u=
l></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Crea=
te Output Shared Memory:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown=
-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Creates </span><code>Local\CognitiveFW_Verdict=
Export</code><span class=3D"">.</span></p></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-=
paragraph"><span class=3D"">Allocates circular buffer for serialized </span=
><code>VerdictRecord</code><span class=3D""> protobufs.</span></p></li></ul=
></li><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Load =
Model Manifest:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragrap=
h"><span class=3D"">Reads </span><code>model_manifest.json</code><span clas=
s=3D"">. Verifies expected input shape </span><code>[4, 32, 32]</code><span=
 class=3D"">. If Layer 3 misconfiguration produced wrong dimensions, the se=
rvice refuses to start and logs a FATAL error.</span></p></li></ul></li><li=
><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong><span class=3D"">Spawn Threads:=
</span></strong><span class=3D""> Batch Collector, GPU Inference, XAI Proce=
ssor, Verdict Dispatcher.</span></p></li></ol><h3><span class=3D"">Phase B:=
 Dynamic Batching (Batch Collector Thread)</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdo=
wn-paragraph"><span class=3D"">Dynamic batching is the most critical perfor=
mance optimization. It trades minimal latency for massive throughput.</span=
