<span class=3D"">6. Reactive TCP RST Injection</span></h2><p class=3D"ds-ma=
rkdown-paragraph"><span class=3D"">When a flow is actively passing traffic =
and Layer 5 retroactively issues a BLOCK verdict, simply dropping future pa=
ckets leaves the connection half-open. The endpoints will wait for timeouts=
. </span><strong><span class=3D"">TCP RST injection</span></strong><span cl=
ass=3D""> cleanly terminates both sides.</span></p><h3><span class=3D"">RST=
 Injection Architecture</span></h3><p class=3D"ds-markdown-paragraph"><span=
 class=3D"">TCP RST injection cannot be done from eBPF (which can only DROP=
/PASS). It requires a separate kernel component: an </span><strong><span cl=
ass=3D"">NDIS Filter Driver</span></strong><span class=3D""> or the </span>=
<strong><span class=3D"">Windows Packet Filter (WinpkFilter)</span></strong=
><span class=3D""> driver.</span></p><div class=3D"md-code-block md-code-bl=
