></div></div></div></div></div><pre><span>Pseudo-code for RST construction:=
</span>
<span>1. Extract SEQ and ACK numbers from the last seen packet in the flow<=
/span>
<span>2. For the RST to the client:</span>
<span>   - src_ip =3D original server IP</span>
<span>   - dst_ip =3D original client IP</span>
<span>   - src_port =3D original server port</span>
<span>   - dst_port =3D original client port</span>
<span>   - SEQ =3D original server SEQ (or client ACK)</span>
<span>   - Flags =3D RST + ACK</span>
<span>   - Recalculate TCP checksum</span>
<span>   - Recalculate IP checksum</span>
<span>3. For the RST to the server (bidirectional):</span>
<span>   - Swap src/dst IPs and ports</span>
<span>   - SEQ =3D original client SEQ (or server ACK)</span>
<span>   - Same process</span>
<span>4. Inject both packets via WinpkFilter NDIS send path</span></pre><sv=
